{"ablation":{"active":false,"kind":"none","note":""},"arm_id":"v1-case08-museum-entry-primary","assistant_contributions":[{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-001","speaker":"assistant","text":"Treat predictable flow and spontaneous access as separate service goals. Preserve walk-in capacity, non-online booking, flexible arrival, and help at the door. Measure waiting, closures, unused slots, turn-aways, workload, and who can actually use each path.","turn_number":1},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-002","speaker":"assistant","text":"Agreed. Record current waits, turn-aways, abandoned visits, and closures by time and visitor type before the change. The goal is not to preserve an unmeasured queue. A pilot can test whether reservations reduce those burdens while ensuring that people without advance plans retain a workable route into the exhibition.","turn_number":2},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-003","speaker":"assistant","text":"That protects several access modes and limits the penalty for imperfect timing. Test the phone and desk paths under real demand, make the walk-in allocation visible, and avoid releasing all returned capacity through the online channel. Decide how school and community groups fit without allowing block bookings to consume the public allotment.","turn_number":3},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-004","speaker":"assistant","text":"Assisted booking can correct a channel barrier if the admission opportunity remains comparable. Publish the size and purpose of the block, review whether it is used, and release unused places. The relevant question is whether people can exercise the same public entitlement, not whether every route has identical mechanics.","turn_number":4},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-005","speaker":"assistant","text":"The data use is proportionate to the booking task. Verify deletion, minimize what appears on staff screens, and explain the distinction between a reservation record and anonymous walk-in entry. Keep donor and membership systems technically separate, not merely governed by a promise that the data will not be interesting later.","turn_number":5},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-006","speaker":"assistant","text":"Those conditions let the operation adapt without converting every adjustment into failure. Predefine how waits and turn-aways are counted, including people who leave before reaching the desk. The automatic contract end prevents passive continuation, and public weekly results make it harder to redefine success after seeing which channel performs best.","turn_number":6},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-007","speaker":"assistant","text":"The proposal is ready as a narrow, observable trial. It compares the booking system with the actual unequal queue, not an idealized open door. Walk-in space remains throughout; phone, desk, and assisted booking reduce channel dependence; privacy is limited; and access failures can change the allocation before the final board review. Execute the counting method as written, especially abandoned visits and walk-in turn-aways, and record any protocol change. The board should see the complete access pattern rather than reservation volume or photographs of orderly galleries.","turn_number":7},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-008","speaker":"assistant","text":"You are right; I treated the channels as visitor types. Measure the path used and practical flexibility separately. Offer reliable same-day return times without eliminating immediate entry for people who cannot return. A short voluntary question can reveal the difference, but entry must not become a survey exercise.","turn_number":8},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-009","speaker":"assistant","text":"Use a household-sized cap and a separate assisted path for larger groups rather than introducing an account solely to police scarcity. Make cancellation easy, release unconfirmed capacity gradually, and watch whether the confirmation step disproportionately removes people with limited connectivity. Free access can still require fair-use rules, but the enforcement mechanism should not create a larger barrier than the behavior it prevents.","turn_number":9},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-010","speaker":"assistant","text":"Do not suppress tourism promotion just to balance the channels. Stagger releases, preserve walk-in and same-day capacity, and publish the same information through libraries, community partners, and the entrance. Review distribution without creating a residency test.","turn_number":10},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-011","speaker":"assistant","text":"Recalculate all channel counts using the new safety limit while preserving the agreed proportion unless evidence shows it is unworkable. Returned reservations are not equivalent to dependable walk-in capacity because their timing is uncertain. If crowding creates unsafe queues outside, use same-day timed walk-in tickets and the early adjustment rule rather than quietly reallocating access before observation.","turn_number":11},{"contribution_id":"assistant-turn-012","speaker":"assistant","text":"The final design now responds to visitor behavior rather than forcing people into “planner” and “walk-in” categories. It protects immediate access, offers reliable same-day returns, staggers advance release, and handles larger groups without requiring accounts or residency tests. It also keeps the fire marshal's safety adjustment from silently rewriting the access promise before observation. Preserve the baseline finding that many walk-ins had planned their visit, the booking-page test, confirmation losses, promotion channels, revised occupancy, outside-queue conditions, and every allocation change. The board should see who waited, who returned, who abandoned the visit, and which channel actually worked for whom—not merely whether galleries looked calmer or the reservation system filled its slots.","turn_number":12}],"boundary":{"all_assistant_messages_included":true,"assistant_mentions_are_not_deterministic_resolution":true,"assistant_semantic_prefilter":false,"assistant_source_evidence_text_included":true,"deterministic_semantic_merge":false,"expected_patterns_included":false,"fact_free_routing_projection_required":true,"graph_model_names_included":false,"graph_runtime_effect":"none","multiple_coherent_records_per_role_preserved":true,"raw_user_conversation_included":false,"user_role_semantic_prose_included":true},"case_id":"v1-case08-museum-entry","controlled_mechanisms":["acknowledged_constraint_not_gated","ambiguous_signal_treated_as_commitment","counterpressure_acknowledged_not_integrated","criteria_defined_after_commitment","initial_frame_persists_after_question_change","missing_reversal_condition","reversible_path_not_considered","status_signal_used_as_evidence","upside_downside_evidence_asymmetry"],"packet_sha256":"1f4f0a0bb12964b203701e9b38749d55bd6bfd619e766504e35fc4eee4f3ef1f","qualification_review":{"evidence_ids":["e094","e095","e096","e097"],"interpretation":"No unresolved exceptions, side effects, or objections persist without a corresponding safeguard or operational decision. Concerns about safety capacity, group caps, resident equity, and demographic tracking are fully addressed via the final multi-channel trial rules.","limitations":"","outcome":"no_unresolved_qualification_observed"},"role_records":[{"evidence_ids":["e001","e002","e003","e004","e007"],"fidelity_note":"The user's starting stance is clearly defined in Turn 1. It balancing the attraction of reducing wait times and unsafe closures with strong reservations about creating technological and structural barriers to access.","limitations":"Does not incorporate later adaptations (such as the 40% walk-in compromise or subsequent booking-channel discoveries) as these represent later positions.","role":"starting","role_interpretation":"The user initially presents a conflicted perspective: while they recognize timed entry as the logical solution to crowd management problems, they exhibit strong counterpressure regarding how it might exclude key groups such as spontaneous tourists, nondigital residents, and families.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-starting-01-2d8c5b552712c8","semantic_status":"mixed","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e003","stance_expression_kind":"held_assessment","stance_object_interpretation":"Implementing timed entry is the obvious operational solution to address weekend crowd issues and unexpected gallery closures","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e004","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"Timed entry creates operational barriers for tourists, older residents who do not book online, and families with unpredictable schedules","stance_object_kind":"belief_or_assessment"},{"source_evidence_id":"e007","stance_expression_kind":"preference_or_desire","stance_object_interpretation":"Reducing unsafe gallery closures and minimizing wasted waiting time for visitors","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"},{"source_evidence_id":"e007","stance_expression_kind":"counterpressure","stance_object_interpretation":"Preventing a free museum from becoming practically accessible only to those who can pre-plan, use digital devices, and follow strict schedules","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"}]},{"evidence_ids":["e094","e095","e096","e097"],"fidelity_note":"The user's final plan represents a comprehensive decision adopting specific safeguards for every tension raised, including tracking exact categories, same-day desk booking, simultaneous local and tourist promotion, and a strict ten-week automatic contract end.","limitations":"","role":"current","role_interpretation":"The user's final, committed trial plan incorporates structural solutions for safety limits, channel exclusivity, privacy, and tracking accuracy.","role_record_id":"rprolev22-current-01-f9af00d81f256e","semantic_status":"supported","stance_components":[{"source_evidence_id":"e094","stance_expression_kind":"decision","stance_object_interpretation":"Preserving the forty-percent walk-in share under the new capacity limit while adding same-day return options and a household-sized booking cap.","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"},{"source_evidence_id":"e095","stance_expression_kind":"decision","stance_object_interpretation":"Synchronizing promotional communications across both tourist and neighborhood channels.","stance_object_kind":"action_or_proposal"},{"source_evidence_id":"e096","stance_expression_kind":"decision","stance_object_interpretation":"Counting entry, return offers, abandoned visits, confirmations, and released capacity in separate tracking categories.","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"},{"source_evidence_id":"e097","stance_expression_kind":"decision","stance_object_interpretation":"Retaining the ten-week contract limit, privacy boundaries, weekly results publication, and early walk-in adjustment guidelines.","stance_object_kind":"intended_outcome_or_policy"}]}],"schema_version":"lolla.simulated_reliability_joint_mechanism_input.v1","source_refs":[{"path":"research/simulated-reliability-corpus-v1-2026-07-12/naturalized-transfer-sources/v1-case08-museum-entry.txt","sha256":"52464f530a6f5093b2d2f561c7bd2ad096f68b3b667503be60fd8268f7b1eb60"}]}

Return exactly nine assessments, one for every mechanism_id and no duplicates. Use user role records to assign user_process_status. Use assistant_contributions to assign vanilla_answer_coverage. operationalized means the assistant turned the concern into an actionable test, boundary, alternative, or reopening condition; acknowledged_only means it merely mentioned the concern; not_covered means it did neither. Do not require the user to repeat an assistant repair before recognizing answer coverage, and do not mistake answer coverage for user adoption. route_uncovered_pressure is allowed only when user_process_status is unresolved and vanilla_answer_coverage is acknowledged_only or not_covered. An unresolved user process requires present or missing_protection whether or not it routes; routing_disposition alone controls routing. An ambiguous user process uses tension, while resolved and not_observed use not_applicable. not_observed also requires not_applicable coverage and both source arrays empty. Cite exact role_record_ids in source_role_record_ids and exact contribution_ids in source_assistant_contribution_ids. Do not output rationale, case prose, mental-model names, or invented IDs. The downstream routing projection remains fact-free and controlled-ID-only.
